<BaseLayout title="Dance & creative movement — Ruijie Wu" description="Exploring movement as expression, imagination and relationship — not as a performance to get right.">
<section class="page-intro container"><a class="back-link" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}practice/`}>← Practice</a><span class="eyebrow">Practice / Movement</span><h1>Movement opens<br /><em>another language.</em></h1><p class="lede">Exploring movement as expression, imagination and relationship — not as a performance to get right.</p></section>
<section class="container detail-body"><div class="prose"><p>Dance and creative movement can create opportunities to notice personal movement qualities, explore space and rhythm, and encounter different ways of relating to oneself and others.</p><p>Group experiences may include body awareness, guided movement exploration, improvisation, movement narratives and reflection. Activities are adapted to the group and setting.</p><p>No assumption of dance skill is made. Participants are invited to work within their own comfort and capacity; observing or pausing are also valid forms of participation.</p></div><aside class="detail-aside"><span class="eyebrow">Related areas</span><p>Psychotherapy · Embodiment · Movement</p><a class="text-link" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}workshops/`}>Explore workshops <span>↗</span></a></aside></section>
<section class="practice-note"><div class="container practice-note-grid"><span class="eyebrow">Continue the conversation</span><div class="prose"><p>For questions about this area of work, current format or possible collaboration, you are welcome to get in touch.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}contact/`}>Contact <span>↗</span></a></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>